These commands are manual-only, so Claude does not start a deployment on its own.

## Hosted MCP server

The plugin configures one `{{ name }}` server at `https://mcp.appwrite.io/`. It provides tools for working with your {{ spec.info.title }} organizations and projects, and for searching the latest {{ spec.info.title }} documentation.

The hosted server uses browser-based OAuth, so the plugin does not require an API key, project ID, endpoint, or other manually configured secret. In a Claude Code session, open `/mcp`, select the `{{ name }}` server, and choose **Authenticate**. From your shell, run:

```sh
claude mcp login plugin:{{ name }}:{{ name }}
```

After authentication, try:

> Use {{ spec.info.title }} to show my workspace context and list my projects.

If authentication expires, choose **Re-authenticate** from `/mcp` or run the login command again. If the browser does not open, use the URL printed by Claude Code. Run `claude mcp get plugin:{{ name }}:{{ name }}` to check the server's authentication and connection status.

